Asset Licensing Policy
======================

Source code in this repository is licensed under the MIT License; see LICENSE.
This file covers everything else — art, audio, fonts, and other non-code assets,
principally under `assets/`.

Every bundled asset is CC0 1.0 Universal (public domain dedication). You may copy,
modify, distribute, and use them — including commercially — without permission and
without attribution. Per-asset provenance (source URL, author, license, retrieval
date) is recorded in ASSETS.md.

If you ship a game built on this starter, you owe nothing: no credits line, no
license file, no bookkeeping. That is the entire point.

What may never be committed here
--------------------------------

- CC BY — attribution-required licences are excluded deliberately. They are fine
  licences; they just push an obligation onto every game built with this starter,
  which defeats the purpose of a starter kit.
- CC BY-NC, CC BY-ND (non-commercial or no-derivatives)
- GPL / AGPL / any copyleft licence
- Marketplace EULAs (Fab, Unity Asset Store, Unreal) — these forbid redistributing
  the raw asset files, which is exactly what a public repository does
- Any licence with a no-redistribution-in-collections clause. A starter kit *is* a
  collection; "Custom CC0 with restrictions" is not CC0.
- Anything of unverified origin

On user-upload sites such as Freesound and OpenGameArt, licences are self-declared
and can be wrong. Our defence is provenance, not licence text — hence the retrieval
date in ASSETS.md, and the CI check that every file under `assets/` has a row there.

